{
 "id": "pair_view",
 "label": "Pair View",
 "category": "Purrmiere",
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "Named crop regions of one picture (two players in a split screen recording, a Discord call). A keyframeable view picks which region fills the frame, or every region shows at once in a grid. Each region has an offset that moves its picture and its sound in time, so a region recorded late can be lined up. Edit the regions in Effect Controls, place them on the picture with the Program monitor, and line them up with Sync regions. Each region can also sit inside a frame of your own, any picture with a see-through middle, with its own zoom inside that frame, and each region's name can be drawn on or under its frame.",
